Other database packages have an `error` scenario; without one `error.type`, `db.response.status_code` and error status on HBase spans aren't measured. Maybe add one, e.g. a `Get` on a missing table:

```suggestion
  batch:
    run: otel-conformance-java run hbase:native HbaseNativeScenario batch

  error:
    run: otel-conformance-java run hbase:native HbaseNativeScenario error
```

```java
case "error":
  error(connection);
  break;

private static void error(Connection connection) throws IOException {
  try (Table missing = connection.getTable(TableName.valueOf("conformance:missing"))) {
    missing.get(new Get(Bytes.toBytes("seed")));
    throw new IllegalStateException("expected TableNotFoundException");
  } catch (TableNotFoundException expected) {
    // expected
  }
}
```

(plus a matching `error` entry in `contracts/hbase.yaml`)
